OL,3,GNEWSAI saved a stranger's life and my
OL,4,Ahusband's at the same time
OL,5,
OL,6,FBy saving a stranger's life, Una Brown
OL,7,Falso saved her husband's.
OL,9,FSean Brown was living with kidney
OL,10,Ffailure and needed a transplant, but
OL,11,FUna was not a 100% match.
OL,13,FThe Belfast couple jumped at the chance
OL,14,Fto take part in the UK Living Kidney
OL,15,FSharing Scheme, which saw Una donate to
OL,16,Fa stranger, enabling Sean to receive a
OL,17,Fcompatible organ from a different
OL,18,Fdonor.
OL,20,F"When I was told that I wasn't a 100%
OL,21,Fmatch, you're automatically thinking,
OL,22,F'God, what's going to happen next?'
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
